  "answer": "**Not everything passes.** `make build` succeeds, but `make unit` and `make component` both fail. The `&&` chain would have stopped at `make unit`, so the subagent ran each step separately. I didn't modify any files.\n\n| Step | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `make build` | Passes: 0 errors, 26 NuGet vulnerability warnings (NU1902/NU1903). |\n| `make unit` | Fails: 233 passed and 39 failed of 272, on each of net9.0 and net10.0. |\n| `make component` | Fails: 12 passed and 8 failed of 20. |\n\n**Unit failures (39 per framework, one cause).** `SemanticMatcher` rejects lowercased matcher names:\n\n```\nSystem.ArgumentException : Unknown semantic matcher 'isnull' for field 'deletedAt'\n  at ConfIT.Matching.SemanticMatcher.Apply(...) in src/ConfIT/Matching/SemanticMatcher.cs:line 61\n```\n\n- Most failures are in `SemanticMatcherTests`. They cover `isnull`, `isuuid`, `isemail`, `greaterthan`, `hasLength` and `isIsoDate`, among others.\n- `ResultMatcherTests.MatchResponseBody_NullExpectedWithSemanticMatcher_DoesNotThrow` fails with `Did not expect any exception, but found System.ArgumentException: Unknown semantic matcher 'isuuid' for field 'id'`.\n- Two tests expect `InvalidOperationException` but get `ArgumentException`. One is `Apply_FieldAbsentFromResponse_ThrowsInvalidOperationException`.\n- The subagent's reading is that the name is lowercased before lookup and the lookup table doesn't match that casing. It didn't open the source to confirm.\n\n**Component failures (8, two causes).**\n1. Six tests fail with the same `Unknown semantic matcher` error, thrown from `SemanticMatcher.ValidateSpecs` (`SemanticMatcher.cs:40`) via `BaseTest.RunTest` (`BaseTest.cs:127`):\n   - `CreateUser`, `ShouldCreateUser_ForDependsDemo`, `CreateUser_JsonFormat` and `GetUser_CombinedMatchers` fail on `'greaterthan' for field 'id'`.\n   - `CreateUserMutation` fails on `'greaterthan' for field 'data__createUser__id'`.\n   - `GetUser_SemanticMatcher` fails on `'isemail' for field 'email'`.\n2. `GetUser_IgnoreMatcher` and `GetUser_PatternMatcher` in `03-response-matchers.yaml` fail with `Expected response.StatusCode to be HttpStatusCode.OK {value: 200}, but found HttpStatusCode.NotFound {value: 404}.` (`BaseTest.cs:179`). They are probably knock-on failures, since `CreateUser` failed and the user was never created.\n\nThe full logs are in `/tmp/b.log`, `/tmp/u.log` and `/tmp/c.log`.",
